WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.600
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.360
What in the world is that?

12
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.280
What incredible Haki!

13
00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.790
We’d better get out of here, fast!

14
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.220
Zoro! This fight is over, let’s go!

15
00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.350
He ain’t gone down yet...

16
00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.540
Jinbe!

17
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.420
Sanji?!

18
00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.710
You have that idiot yet?

19
00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.220
Handling it now!

20
00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.430
We’re going, Zoro!
Call it a win for you!

21
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.610
Sorry, Rob Lucci...

22
00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.280
Fishman Karate:

23
00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.400
Five Thousand Brick...

24
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.110
...Chop!

25
00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.060
Cipher Pol “Aigis” Zero...

26
00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.520
Rob Lucci.

27
00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.110
Where is York?

28
00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.200
We’ve got to hurry!

29
00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:58.820
Hey...

30
00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.820
What the hell is that?!

31
00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:08.040
York is still being held captive in the control room
on the fourth floor of Building A.

32
00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.590
The two who just fled from here...

33
00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:15.510
...were Roronoa Zoro
and First Son of the Sea Jinbe.

34
00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:20.260
And five of the Straw Hats,

35
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.220
along with two of the Vegapunks,

36
00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:25.640
are preparing to escape
at the rear entrance of the Labophase.

37
00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:30.690
There are also 85 Cipher Pol agents...

38
00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.610
...and four Seraphim
in the basement of the lab.

39
00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.650
Vegapunk’s broadcast resumes
in six minutes.

40
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.040
Well done.

41
00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.500
I have no further questions for you.

42
00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.380
One more thing...!

43
00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:07.810
My partner’s seriously injured,
he should still be in the control room...

44
00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.190
Please, spare him!

45
00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.690
That will prove difficult...

46
00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:22.360
One does not attempt to step on insects...
It simply happens.

47
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.290
You’re as...

48
00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.500
...strong as ever,

49
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.800
you big ol’ Giants, you!

50
00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.460
Straw Hat!

51
00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:42.590
I hardly recognized ya!

52
00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:49.270
How do you know the appearance of
Elbaf’s god of legend?!

53
00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:53.310
Your outfit pleases us greatly!

54
00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:01.190
I dunno whatcha mean by that,
but let’s catch up later!

55
00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.160
The Giants!

56
00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.620
A most unpleasant combination!

57
00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:17.040
Those are some humongous beasts!

58
00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.250
Just like the savage beasts
in the forests of Elbaf!

59
00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:22.220
Hey, big guy!

60
00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:26.430
We don’t wanna fight ‘em!
We gotta get outta here!

61
00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.550
Oh, we know!

62
00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.600
We just ran into Sanji!

63
00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.270
Hueh?!

64
00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:35.480
He said, “If you see Luffy,
tell him to run around the back of the island”!

65
00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.980
Dorry, Brogy! Counting on you two!

66
00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.320
You got it!

67
00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.440
We’ll see you later!

68
00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.700
We read about you in the newspaper
and came to help you all escape!

69
00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:52.830
It said you were surrounded
by the Navy!

70
00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:59.070
Zoro &
Jinbe
Luffy & Giants
Current location
Elbaf ship
Sanji &
Vegapunk
Bonney
 and the rest
Nami, Usopp 
and the rest

71
00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:57.500
Egghead,
surrounded by the Navy...

72
00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:01.590
This is how the Straw Hats
are currently scattered about.

73
00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.990
Elbaf ship
Bonney
 and the rest
Luffy & Giants
Current location

74
00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.320
Nami, Usopp 
and the rest

75
00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:03.450
Sanji &
Vegapunk

76
00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.900
Zoro &
Jinbe

77
00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:05.490
Elbaf ship
Bonney
 and the rest
Luffy & Giants
Current location

78
00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:05.470
Let’s head back to the ship, then!

79
00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.490
Sanji &
Vegapunk

80
00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.090
We’d better let everyone know!

81
00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:25.860
Looks like the Bosses
met up with Straw Hat!

82
00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:29.160
Back to the ship!
Prepare to withdraw!

83
00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.330
Aye!

84
00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.740
We should just make
our way back with them!

85
00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.120
We could plunder their battleships,
but we won’t find treasure aboard!

86
00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.290
You ain’t wrong!

87
00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.090
Dammit!

88
00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:46.220
Is that their signal to escape?

89
00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.220
That presents a problem.

90
00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:52.180
I must sound a warning of my own, then...

91
00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:54.270
A warning not to escape!

92
00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.710
The island’s pulsing again!

93
00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:24.590
Hey!

94
00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.680
Whaaaa?!

95
00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:43.340
<b>Sun-Shield</b>

96
00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:49.240
Man, that freaked me out...
Almost lost ‘em!

97
00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:51.570
There.

98
00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.790
You okay, Straw Hat?!

99
00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.380
Got all your bits ‘n pieces back?

100
00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:04.540
Yeah, thanks!

101
00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:09.420
You’ve got quite the
hilarious body now!

102
00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.430
And you look
stronger than ever, to boot!

103
00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.640
Ya think so?

104
00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.930
Anyway...

105
00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:16.970
Yeah...

106
00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:20.060
That Conqueror’s roar...

107
00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:24.190
Who’s he supposed to be?

108
00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:27.280
Some uppity World Government guy!

109
00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:33.910
Brogy!

110
00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:34.990
Yeah!

111
00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:40.410
Svalinn Sun-Shield!

112
00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.590
We have much to settle with your kind...

113
00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:52.090
Do you not understand
the likes of who he is?!

114
00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:53.880
Yeah!

115
00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.550
Of course we do!

116
00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:56.550
He’s our friend!

117
00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:02.020
Skilja Split!

118
00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.200
Your friend?

119
00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.490
Nonsense.

120
00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:21.370
I care not for the relationships
of insects that band together...

121
00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.080
And before you call him something else,

122
00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.540
he must be crushed!

123
00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:34.630
Removed from the historical record...

124
00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:36.970
...for good!

125
00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:41.160
Those’re totally poisonous!
Don’t touch ‘em!

126
00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.000
Charge!

127
00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.920
Charge!

128
00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:24.520
How d’ya like a taste of
yer own poison?!

129
00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.230
What?! They exploded!

130
00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:39.660
Bosses!
The fire’s gonna block off the forest!

131
00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.910
Right, let’s get moving!

132
00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:42.620
You blew ‘em to bits!

133
00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:45.000
Better hurry, better hurry!

134
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.710
They’re unkillable, after all!

135
00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.760
What do you mean, “unkillable”?

136
00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.890
How should I know?! No matter
what we do, they just keep comin’ back!

137
00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:04.220
I’ve never heard of that kind of power,
or of any race that has it!

138
00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.690
Best get runnin’, then!

139
00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.310
Run!

140
00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.190
All right, we’re almost there!

141
00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.530
We’d be there faster
if you’d help, dammit!

142
00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:21.490
Hurry up, Jinbe, Zoro!

143
00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.530
I hear you, we’ll be right there!

144
00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:29.500
It’s faster to just run!

145
00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.460
Hey, look at that!

146
00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:35.920
In front of the ship!

147
00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.430
You won’t be boarding this ship,
Jewelry Bonney!

148
00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.600
There’s that real bad feeling...

149
00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.890
Let... me... oooout!

150
00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:50.850
Uh?

151
00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:03.200
It’s a monsteeeer!

152
00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.950
Where is the room on the monitor?

153
00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.660
It talked!

154
00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:10.920
Who’re you?!
Just go awaaaay!

155
00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:21.050
Kizaru, sir!
You must let us treat you!

156
00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:22.640
Show us your wounds!

157
00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.350
I certainly have a wound...

158
00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:27.930
And it runs deep...

159
00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:31.810
Then we need to act fast!
Where are you hurt?!

160
00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:37.070
Just let me rest...

161
00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.080
Joyboy...

162
00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:19.230
Northwest coast of Egghead,
reporting in!

163
00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:23.570
Something far larger than the Giants
has appeared on the island!

164
00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:27.950
The fire isn’t affecting it at all!

165
00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.500
The giant creature
standing in the fire...

166
00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.580
...seems to be groaning
about something...

167
00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:46.260
Sorry...

168
00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:53.020
Sorry, Joyboy...

169
00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.580
All Pacifista Mk. IIIs have been incapacitated!

170
00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:25.380
I want more pressure on Egghead!
More shells!

171
00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:29.470
You will not let Emperor
Straw Hat’s crew escape!

172
00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.980
You will not let Jewelry Bonney get away!

173
00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:39.860
A mere twelve-year-old girl...

174
00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:44.070
...and you gave her the power
to destroy an entire country?

175
00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:47.990
A foolish way to go about
committing treason, Vegapunk!

176
00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:53.490
Hurry, back to the ship!

177
00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:56.870
Some insanely tough guys
just came ashore!

178
00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.420
Don’t let them sail out!

179
00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:03.880
Sink the Elbaf ship!

180
00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:06.340
Make for the northeast shore!

181
00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:11.260
This is far as you criminals go!

182
00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:14.810
Max Power!

183
00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:16.890
Damn roadblock!

184
00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:19.600
You will not pass!

185
00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:21.400
Outta the way!

186
00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:26.190
Strong...

187
00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:28.450
Steam...

188
00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.330
...Right!

189
00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.580
...Knuc—oobph!

190
00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.000
Jewelry Bonney!

191
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.340
Brace yourself!

192
00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:46.510
Look after my Daddy, Giant!

193
00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.720
Sure! He’s in good hands!

194
00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:51.180
Jewelry Bonney, you snot-nosed brat!

195
00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:54.260
I’m not gonna let you have
those weapons!

196
00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:02.770
Don’t call my father a weapon!

197
00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:03.730
Cra—

198
00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:13.070
D-Don’t...!

199
00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.040
My Daddy is a hero,

200
00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.120
you big-chinned old fart!

201
00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.210
Take it back!

202
00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:32.970
Stop it! This just looks wrong!

203
00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.580
Labophase

204
00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:49.690
I can’t help but notice
you’re not drinking your Vega Coffee.

205
00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:52.910
It was too hot!
I’ve got a sensitive tongue, you know!

206
00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:56.200
That’s mean of you, Shaka.
You know he can’t handle hot things...

207
00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.160
Four minutes to go, Stella.

208
00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.790
Oh, yes, right.

209
00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:04.630
Yeowhot!

210
00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.050
Are you certain that it is this room?

211
00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:19.060
I’m pretty sure this’s where
they were recording...

212
00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:25.900
Uh?

213
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.250
Uweh?!
Hold on!

214
00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.170
Wait, wait! Don’t do anythin’ crazy!

215
00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:55.800
Stella, there is not much time...

216
00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.050
See? You didn’t stop a thing!

217
00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.260
Using a thermoelectric element,

218
00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:04.020
if we cool down the coffee
 by converting heat energy...

219
00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:12.650
Even I’d hide the Transponder Snail
sendin’ out the signal somewhere else, if I was Stella!

220
00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:15.200
Then I shall simply destroy the entire lab.

221
00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:17.200
Not an option!

222
00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:21.450
The second floor of Building B’s for weapons development.

223
00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.540
And the first floor is a power plant.

224
00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:24.960
The third floor of Building C’s...

225
00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:27.580
...where we keep rows of
high-pressure gas cylinders.

226
00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:31.340
If any of ‘em are destroyed,
it’ll set off everything in the lab,

227
00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:35.970
and the lab’ll go boom
along with Punk Records!

228
00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:38.010
If that is so, then ponder!

229
00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:40.890
You, too, ought to share
his neural pathways!

230
00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:44.600
Of course I’m gonna stop this
big, dumb broadcast.

231
00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:49.020
If they keep committin’ crimes,
it makes it that much harder for me to get in with yous.

232
00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:53.360
Whatsa matter?

233
00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:57.910
I sense the voice of a small creature.

234
00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.240
In Punk Records?

235
00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.200
Oh! Could it be a Transponder Snail?

236
00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:07.920
The Transmission Transponder Snail
was cooked up just recently.

237
00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:12.170
It’s got a cone-like spiral shell, like this.

238
00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.670
You will guide me to the entrance.

239
00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:33.230
Good for you.
Looks like you were beneath his notice.

240
00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:36.190
Both of us were.

241
00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:38.900
Still, what was that monster?

242
00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:42.530
Judging from the conversation,
one of the Five Elders, I’d reckon.

243
00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:46.540
Thought as much.
Pretty off-putting transformation he’s got.

244
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.540
Did they abandon you, Stussy?

245
00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.510
After you took the trouble to
stab us in the back, poor thing...

246
00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:58.220
I hate to disappoint you,

247
00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.510
but I chose to stay here.

248
00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:07.100
Someone has to carry out
the final mission.

249
00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:11.650
What?!

250
00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.900
Then we’re leaving Stussy behind?!

251
00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:18.740
Ain’t nothin’ doin’ ‘bout it!
Da barrier’s gotta go down da moment da ship can get out!

252
00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.820
Da Frontier Dome can only be deactivated
from da control room.

253
00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:24.120
She volunteered!

254
00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:29.080
Ain’t thankin’ her and den us gettin’ out
da best way to repay her?

255
00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:32.170
You bet I’m going to put everything I’ve got into running away, but...

256
00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:34.670
Robin...

257
00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:37.750
We might lower the barrier,
all thanks to her,

258
00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:41.760
but we aren’t capable of flying as far as
Vegaforce-01 was supposed to carry us...

259
00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:43.760
Dat’s right, Nico Robin.

260
00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:47.060
Ah mathed it out.
Based on basic physics,

261
00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:50.180
dis ship’s definitely
gonna to fall to da ground!

262
00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:51.690
Whaaaa?!

263
00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:52.940
Whaaaah?!

264
00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:56.730
Hey, the Coup De Burst is ready for use!

265
00:21:57.230 --> 00:22:01.070
Once Zoro and Jinbe get here,
we’ll make a super jump towards the sea!

266
00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:02.740
We’ve got a big problem!

267
00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:06.030
We need more than just the Coup De Burst
to reach the sea!

268
00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:08.240
Whaaaa?!

269
00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:13.290
If it looks like we won’t be able to reach the sea,
then I know your strength’ll carry us through!

270
00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:19.000
Must be hard bein’ your ship!

271
00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:21.920
But Ah like dat can-do attitude!

272
00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:24.930
It’s always dat kind o’ strength
dat makes miracles!

273
00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:27.600
And dat’s comin’ from a scientist!

274
00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:31.810
Ah’ll make sure yer ship
lands on da water safely!

275
00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:36.400
Trust me!

276
00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:40.900
Edison!

277
00:22:42.820 --> 00:22:44.860
Doooon’t!

278
00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:48.370
Y’all absolutely gotta make it outta here,
Straw Hats!

279
00:22:48.950 --> 00:22:52.870
Simulated external damage: 78 percent.

280
00:22:52.870 --> 00:22:55.580
Not enough ta kill me! Let’s go!

281
00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:03.130
Edison!

282
00:23:16.690 --> 00:23:18.060
There's an inward wind...

283
00:23:18.610 --> 00:23:20.690
pulling us toward the island!

284
00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:38.880
This is some crazy suction!

285
00:23:38.880 --> 00:23:41.170
Goin’ forward ain’t happening!

286
00:23:54.350 --> 00:23:55.560
Ya big jerk!

287
00:24:23.630 --> 00:24:26.630
If yer that hungry,

288
00:24:29.220 --> 00:24:32.600
chow down on some buildings!

289
00:24:57.120 --> 00:24:58.790
That’s the stuff!

290
00:25:00.580 --> 00:25:01.710
Aw, crud...

291
00:25:02.250 --> 00:25:05.750
Losing... my... strength...

292
00:25:08.130 --> 00:25:10.220
That was a good one!

293
00:25:18.350 --> 00:25:20.390
I’m pooped...

294
00:25:20.770 --> 00:25:22.480
Whaaaa?!

295
00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:26.070
What’s happened to you, Straw Hat?!
You’ve turned into some old stranger!

296
00:25:26.070 --> 00:25:29.990
All... outta... food power...

297
00:25:29.990 --> 00:25:32.860
Food? You want some Hákarl?

298
00:25:33.110 --> 00:25:35.410
Hákarl?

299
00:25:35.410 --> 00:25:36.830
This.

300
00:25:42.920 --> 00:25:45.500
What’s this smell?

301
00:25:45.750 --> 00:25:49.760
It’s fermented shark.
Elbaf’s emergency rations!

302
00:25:58.390 --> 00:26:00.480
Eat up, now!

303
00:26:03.100 --> 00:26:05.560
It’s good once you get used to it.

304
00:26:10.530 --> 00:26:12.150
Oh, yeah!

305
00:26:12.150 --> 00:26:14.740
Smelled nasty, but my energy’s back!

306
00:26:16.700 --> 00:26:18.700
Your body works in simple ways!

307
00:26:19.870 --> 00:26:22.460
Now you’re back to your old self!

308
00:26:28.590 --> 00:26:30.340
Look out! The boar’s coming!

309
00:26:37.010 --> 00:26:38.350
Chew on this!

310
00:26:38.350 --> 00:26:40.020
Gear 3:

311
00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:50.030
Gum-Gum...

312
00:26:50.030 --> 00:26:51.320
...Red...

313
00:26:51.900 --> 00:26:52.940
...Roc!

314
00:27:08.130 --> 00:27:11.920
Yowwww!
How freakin’ hard is your body?!

315
00:27:27.520 --> 00:27:29.730
Whoa, hey, yo!
What’s that, what’s that?!

316
00:27:29.730 --> 00:27:30.860
Something’s down there!

317
00:27:32.070 --> 00:27:34.070
Huh?! A crab?!

318
00:28:02.140 --> 00:28:04.560
Stella, one minute to go.

319
00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:06.100
You don’t have to tell me!

320
00:28:17.650 --> 00:28:19.200
This must be it...

321
00:28:19.200 --> 00:28:22.620
Your luck has run out, Vegapunk.

322
00:28:39.780 --> 00:28:44.000
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

323
00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:48.220
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop beep-beep-beep-bup-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipii pipopii, pipopiipii

324
00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:52.430
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

325
00:28:52.430 --> 00:28:54.910
Beep-bup-beep
Piipapii papipo, piipapii

326
00:28:56.840 --> 00:28:59.960
No No No No No norenai

327
00:28:56.840 --> 00:29:00.040
No, no, no, no, no, not feelin' it

328
00:29:00.040 --> 00:29:04.200
kobiritsuichatte mou odorenai

329
00:29:00.050 --> 00:29:04.240
I'm all stiff, all outta dances

330
00:29:04.240 --> 00:29:08.480
My head feels so good, 'f I get unlucky again
atama Feel so good, mata Unlucky demo

331
00:29:08.480 --> 00:29:12.580
Cola de fukitobase yowaki o
just gonna blow away the shy with a cola

332
00:29:12.580 --> 00:29:16.660
Hey all you boys & girls! Looking good!
soko no Boys & Girls! omae ii yatsu

333
00:29:16.660 --> 00:29:20.210
Hey all you boys & girls!
soko no Boys & Girls!

334
00:29:22.050 --> 00:29:24.180
Update failed. I've had enough!
appudeto wa shippai kori gori

335
00:29:24.180 --> 00:29:26.060
Wasn't it OK 'til yesterday?
kinou made nara seikai?

336
00:29:26.060 --> 00:29:32.390
La la la la la la, run, run, run...
ran ran ran ran ran ran Run Run Run

337
00:29:32.390 --> 00:29:36.110
